WEBVTT

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:10.740
Wow...

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.540
It's way bigger than I imagined.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.540
The ancient city of Babylon...

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.780
Ages ago, it was once a prosperous citadel.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.720
Now all that remains are mostly legends.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.950
Legends that devils dwell there, and that it's linked to the land of the dead...

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:29.230
We even have the same kind of stories on the surface.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:30.690
Where is the entrance?

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:35.360
There are four. Each of those towers contains an entrance of its own, but...

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.230
...only one of them connects to Babel.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:43.810
That is, assuming this map from the antique shop is truly legit.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.740
It's in ancient script though.
Does it say anything else, Eljuia?

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.480
Yes.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.910
I think...

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.490
Zhurong, the god of fire and the south.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.120
I believe that tower is the correct entrance.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:18.930
<i>In the city without love</i> <i>only your smile remains.</i>

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:28.940
<i>Hold me tight to crush the loneliness,</i> <i>it's all that stops these pains.</i>

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:39.330
<i>You're constrained by that limit.</i>
<i>Free yourself and break apart the chains.</i>

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:49.330
<i>It's all gonna burn on down.</i>
<i>Dance to the flames that consume the night.</i>

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:59.500
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright.</i>

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:10.030
<i>Dance to the end of the night.</i>

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:20.020
<i>The inferno rages on. It's almost</i> <i>as beautiful as you. Beautiful and bright. Dance!</i>

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:30.700
<i>In the city without love</i>

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.430
There's a key to the gate?

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:48.060
How do we find it if we don't even know what it looks like?

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.600
Demetrio!

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:50.830
Is this it?

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:51.930
That's the key?!

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.370
Most likely.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:05.550
We did it!

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:11.520
"11: Depths"

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:15.620
This path should take us directly to Babel.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.030
Sweet! Let's go!

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.430
Not so fast.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.560
Mischa.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:27.430
If this is the way to Babel, it will probably be trapped.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:29.610
There's nothing there.

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:30.710
Yes, I see that.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.570
I wasn't talking to you.

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:35.230
All right. Let's move!

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.120
These footprints are still fresh.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:50.790
Delzaine and the others...

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.760
They must have beat us here.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:56.900
We need to hurry or it'll be too late!
Is there another door?

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.500
--No.
--Huh?

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:00.940
We'll have to climb this.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.140
What?!

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:05.840
You can't be serious!

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.610
Now we've gotta go rock climbing?

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:09.510
Rock...?

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:14.110
I know! Hey, Falarion? Can you get big again and let us ride you up?

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.150
Don't be ridiculous.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.590
No good?

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:35.970
Are you all right?

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:38.630
Yeah! Don't you worry about me!

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:45.150
Emilio!

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:49.820
You're damn heavy!

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.490
That was close.

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.290
Yeah...

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:59.160
Might have saved my life.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.730
What?

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:03.130
You might have just saved my life.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:05.330
Quit it. It's not like you to say that.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:08.500
Hey! You two!

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.500
Quit screwing around. Hurry up and climb.

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:18.050
We finally made it.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:20.750
It's way too early to relax.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.490
First a wall and now a maze...

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:26.250
These obstacles just keep on coming.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.430
We're all set.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.420
Good. Let's go.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.450
Let me set something straight.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:53.020
I have no intentions of killing Delzaine.

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:55.120
What are you talking about?

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.590
You've built an army of soldiers and Zoozians.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:02.730
True, but... Our revolution will spill no blood.

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:04.460
I've heard you say that.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:05.130
But...

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.730
But what?

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:10.760
Do you really think Delzaine is someone who can be reasoned with?

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:16.770
I know what he's like as a king, but not as a person.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.740
He's a demon! What else do you need to know?!

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:24.110
If he's gone, the Zoozians and all the poor citizens could be saved!

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.550
Isn't that right?!

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:31.720
The kingdom's problems can't be solved by killing the king... or anyone else.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:36.920
The army we've gathered exists only to force Delzaine to surrender the throne.

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:40.650
Why do you want to kill the king?

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:48.900
Isn't it a bit selfish to expect our help without even telling us why?

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.740
You need to explain yourself.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.070
It's for revenge.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:03.090
Delzaine isn't my father.
He killed mine--the former king.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:05.290
I have to avenge him!

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:09.520
I swore to become strong and get even!
And now I have the chance!

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.460
Revenge, huh?

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:16.630
My revolution is revenge as well.

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:21.000
Years ago, a pompous noble killed my Zoozian friend.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:26.810
I trained myself hard just to exact revenge on that noble.

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:34.450
But then... through experience and time,
I learned that wasn't the right path.

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:37.490
Blood can't be washed away with more blood.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:41.960
If I killed that noble, his relatives would come and find me for revenge.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:45.730
It would have borne an endless cycle of violence.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:50.470
That's why my revenge is against this rotten world itself.

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:52.630
That is, in the form of revolution.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:58.640
Let me ask you the same question
I did when we met...

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:02.310
What do you plan to do when the king is dead?

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:05.080
What will become of the kingless kingdom?

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:12.350
In any case, I'll be the one to negotiate with Delzaine first.

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:18.590
Don't you dare draw your sword on him before I have a chance to speak with him.

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:22.400
I... only want revenge.

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:23.830
I see...

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:35.540
Emilio?

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:38.180
Hey, prince.

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:41.410
Before you swing at people, try talking first.

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:55.360
It seems that once we pass this labyrinth, we'll find the path to Babel.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:58.030
I doubt it will go that smoothly.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:00.370
I'll be there to protect Demetrio.

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:02.040
You don't have to say it every time.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.470
Shut up.

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:04.910
Let's move.

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:18.950
Demetrio and the others should have reached Babylon by now.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.990
Do you think they'll make it safely to Babel?

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:24.560
That man most certainly will.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:27.930
Either way, we'll need to prepare the army.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:36.100
We'll be departing shortly!

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:38.270
Everyone gather around!

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:41.000
Demetrio...

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.840
Read the stones... Listen to the wind...

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.850
It's this way.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:06.440
Noxious fumes stir and fill the air.

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:09.170
But this is the only way forward...

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:21.620
It's finally time.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:27.820
No matter what happens, I live to fulfill
Demetrio's ambitions... Nothing else.

00:10:27.820 --> 00:10:30.990
I'll protect Demetrio, even if it means my life.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:38.500
Shun?

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.300
You think Emilio is okay?

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:42.300
Yeah. I dunno...

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:44.510
I think Demetrio said something to him.

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:45.910
Yeah.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.550
Shun. Aren't you glad?

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:51.850
Huh? Why's that?

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:55.880
Because once we reach Babel, you can go back to the surface.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.350
Oh yeah, you're right.

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:02.660
I was so excited when we first got to Babylon, too.

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:05.990
What's so different now?

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:07.430
All right.

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:09.060
Hey, Emilio.

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:13.000
What do you want?

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.270
Um, I...

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:20.840
When we get to Babel,
I might be able to go home and all...

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:24.110
...but before I do, there's that promise I made to you.

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:29.920
Is that promise still standing?
I just wanna make sure...

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:31.350
Get to the point.

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:32.890
I mean, are you still trying to avenge--

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:34.290
We're through.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:43.590
That must be the entrance that takes us to Babel.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:46.900
So that's the--

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:48.300
Hey, wait!

00:11:54.410 --> 00:11:57.550
Allow me to welcome you all to your funeral.

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:59.140
It's an ambush.

00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:17.170
Prince... Let's start with you!

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:18.600
Die!

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:25.570
Gah!

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:26.310
Damn it!

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:28.580
I told you not to kill the prince.

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:30.280
I'm just trying to scare 'em!

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:33.150
You again? You sure are persistent!

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:39.020
Out of my way! I have no vendetta with you!

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:41.820
Even if you don't, I have one with you!

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:45.930
Your opponent is me.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:48.430
You arrived quicker than expected.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:51.930
Unfortunately for you, that just means you'll die sooner.

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:53.340
What a shame.

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:55.470
Well, I'm an impatient man.

00:12:55.470 --> 00:13:00.430
This fight will be over shortly, but it's you who will fall.

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:03.680
I'm Guidoro of the Truculent.

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:06.440
Your name means nothing to me.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:49.420
I need to return you two the favor...

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:56.230
I'll give you both a scar like mine--
No... You'll taste an even greater pain!

00:13:56.230 --> 00:14:01.830
I'll gouge holes in your flesh, pound you to death, and chop you into meat!

00:14:35.070 --> 00:14:37.870
It's over. Stand down and surrender.

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:53.790
Emilio!

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:59.900
You know, the king told us not to kill you.

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:00.800
What?!

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:08.770
Even though you're his son and tried to kill him, Delzaine doesn't want you dead.

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:10.800
But I'm not like him.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:34.700
Die!

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:40.940
What?!

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.270
I don't have time for this!

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:48.300
He's right there! Delzaine is so close!

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.780
Emilio!

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:54.180
You're not getting away!

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:01.280
I won't let you pass.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:15.400
--Emilio!
--Emilio!

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:21.480
You're in for a lot of pain if you get in my way! Move it!

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:23.880
No. I will not.

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:28.480
I can still slow you down, even if I cannot defeat you.

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:29.880
Damn!

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:45.600
You've never been one to follow orders, Ibelda.

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:48.600
Long time no see, Louise.

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:50.200
What's the meaning of this?

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:53.230
You still don't get it?

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:57.710
She's got the blood of the Zoozians running through her.

00:16:57.710 --> 00:17:03.280
Your silly revolution means nothing to her.
Isn't that right, Louise?

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:06.550
Louise? What are you--

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:08.790
It won't change anything anyways.

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:14.230
Half of my blood is that of a Zoozian.

00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:17.800
But thanks to my appearance,
I could live as an Endras.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:21.270
That's the only reason I wasn't discriminated against.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:25.070
But... I knew that something was wrong with the world.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:32.780
My father had talent in medicine and my mother was good at sewing.

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:36.420
They... never had the chance to show their skills.

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:39.120
My father, because he was Zoozian...

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:44.090
...and my mother, because she married a despicable Zoozian...

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:47.820
...were forced into awful work that no Endras wanted to do.

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:52.500
Even as a child, I knew it wasn't right.

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:59.140
Isn't that why you rallied behind
Demetrio and joined the Ignauts?

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:02.680
You still think that?
It's all about money! Money!

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:05.510
I needed money to live!

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:07.740
Don't clump me together with you!

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:13.150
Feeding the Ignauts' movements to the Truculent earns me plenty.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:16.990
That way, I can spare my family from tragedy.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:20.480
Revolution is for people with nothing better to do.

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:23.190
Do it, Louise.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:27.770
Goodbye, Eljuia. You really are a fool.

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:29.870
Wait!

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:31.270
Demetrio!

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:35.040
You'll earn more killing me than Eljuia, right?

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:37.450
What do you say, Louise?

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:41.380
Your revolution will fail. You're a sucker who can't even tell who his allies are.

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:43.370
Shut up, you traitor!

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:47.190
You must really despise me.

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:51.690
I knew it was you who sided with the Truculent.

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:57.860
Our movements were leaked, especially after the prince happened to join us.

00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:01.640
That's why I kept our group so small.

00:19:01.640 --> 00:19:03.740
At first, I wanted to doubt it...

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:09.470
...but when the Truculent ambushed us here,
I knew it was you, Louise.

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:19.420
Fight me for real, Demetrio!

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:22.260
I'm really going to kill you!

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:24.990
If that's how it is, so be it, Louise!

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:26.060
But...

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:28.160
This is wrong!

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:29.500
What is?

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:32.430
I'm not going to help your revenge!

00:19:32.430 --> 00:19:35.170
I was wondering what you'd say.

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:36.200
Are you too scared?

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:36.910
That's not it!

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:38.340
Then why?!

00:19:38.340 --> 00:19:41.370
Just like Demetrio said, you need to talk first!

00:19:43.850 --> 00:19:45.750
Come on, Emilio!

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:50.120
You... You don't understand anything about me.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.550
Emilio...

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:54.920
You're right, I don't! I don't understand one bit!

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:59.050
But that doesn't even matter.
Revenge is never the right choice!

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:06.730
I'm not letting you go.

00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:07.900
Shut up!

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:10.300
Shun!

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:13.370
Emilio!

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:16.580
Ow...

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:17.710
You okay?!

00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:18.650
Yeah.

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:20.880
We've got to stop Emilio!

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:28.290
My lord...

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:30.090
It will begin operation soon.

00:20:30.090 --> 00:20:34.500
The gate of Babel will only stay open for a limited time...

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:36.900
...so once it does, step this way.

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:46.310
At last, I can fulfill my wish of many years...

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:47.740
Delzaine!

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:56.020
Emilio.

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:04.890
"To be continued..."

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:09.630
<i>Took a long way to get here</i>

00:21:09.630 --> 00:21:13.600
<i>Had to go around and around</i>

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:17.710
<i>But every single road I've taken</i>

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:21.610
<i>Made me who I am today</i>

00:21:21.610 --> 00:21:28.540
<i>go my way go my way</i>

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:40.030
<i>The world will show you there's tomorrow</i>

00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:48.560
<i>Look up to the blue sky and you will see</i>

00:21:49.400 --> 00:21:57.480
<i>I try to be better than who I was yesterday</i>

00:21:57.480 --> 00:22:04.650
<i>So I can see you with a smile on my face today</i>

00:22:04.650 --> 00:22:09.890
<i>Now what should we get into today?</i>

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:18.530
<i>The scent of summer arouses my heart</i>

00:22:18.530 --> 00:22:23.670
<i>And I can't seem to find the right words to tell you</i>

00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:28.110
<i>That I love you just the way you are</i>

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:39.910
"Episode 12: The Light of Babel"

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:39.890
Next episode, "The Light of Babel."
